<section>
    <h2>Files go both ways</h2>
    <p>
        Real apps hand you files (invoices, exports, reports) and ask for them (avatars, CSVs, attachments). A test
        can't look in your Downloads folder or click around the system file picker, and it doesn't need to:
        Playwright catches the download before it lands, and fills a file input directly.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Catching a download</h2>
    <p>A download is an event, so start waiting for it before the click that causes it:</p>
<pre><code>var download = await Page.RunAndWaitForDownloadAsync(async () =>
{
    await Page.GetByRole(AriaRole.Link, new() { Name = "Export" }).ClickAsync();
});

Console.WriteLine(download.SuggestedFilename);          // the name the server gave it
var text = await File.ReadAllTextAsync(await download.PathAsync());   // where it was saved
await download.SaveAsAsync("exports/report.csv");        // keep a copy</code></pre>
    <p class="tip">
        <strong>Wait first, click second.</strong> Click first and the download can start and finish before you
        begin listening, and then you wait forever.
    </p>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>Uploading</h2>
    <p>
        <code>SetInputFilesAsync</code> fills a file input. Give it a path, several paths, or a file made in memory,
        so your test doesn't need a fixtures folder:
    </p>
<pre><code>var upload = Page.GetByLabel("Attachment");

await upload.SetInputFilesAsync("fixtures/avatar.png");
await upload.SetInputFilesAsync(new FilePayload
{
    Name = "notes.txt",                     // the name the page sees
    MimeType = "text/plain",
    Buffer = Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes("Hello from a test"),
});
await upload.SetInputFilesAsync(Array.Empty&lt;string&gt;());   // clear it again</code></pre>
    <p>
        When a button opens the picker and the input is hidden, catch the picker instead:
    </p>
<pre><code>var chooser = await Page.RunAndWaitForFileChooserAsync(async () =>
{
    await Page.GetByRole(AriaRole.Button, new() { Name = "Upload" }).ClickAsync();
});
await chooser.SetFilesAsync("fixtures/avatar.png");</code></pre>
</section>

<section>
    <h2>The Courier's Counter</h2>
    <p>
        The Guild trusts paper, not screens. Collect your sealed dispatch, read the seal inside it, and hand back a
        reply with the seal in it, in a file with exactly the name the dispatch asks for. Ten seconds.
    </p>
</section>
